Continued monitoring will show whether

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:31.520
the increased activity persists through the coming weeks.

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:36.360
Comet 220P McNawt remains visible in the pre-don sky

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:38.400
for observers at southern latitudes.

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:42.280
From a fleeting comet, we shift to a month-long record

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:43.560
of two bright planets.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:47.900
The two planets appear to draw nearer in Earth's sky,

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.900
even as their actual orbital distances increased.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:53.960
The composite image captures the changing

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:56.140
angular separation night after night

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:58.180
from a single observing site.

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:00.480
Such alignments occur regularly,

00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:04.040
