00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:13.240
SpaceX's public listing introduces new variables

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:15.700
into long-term planning for agency programs.

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:19.360
Finally, a quiet chemical clue is rewriting

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:22.040
how we think life's ingredients arrived on Earth.

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:25.400
Iron meteorites and conduits show phosphorus

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:28.360
to nitrogen ratios that challenge earlier models

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:30.160
of how Earth acquired these elements.

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:33.380
The work points to Jupiter's early migration

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:35.260
as a key distributor of material

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:37.080
across the young solar system.

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:39.940
Samples from different formation regions

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:42.480
reveal distinct chemical fingerprints preserved

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:44.640
since the protoplanetary disk era.

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:48.200
Further laboratory analysis of additional meteorites

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:50.380
is planned to test the revised timeline.

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:53.640
Iron meteorites that formed closer to the sun

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:56.380
carry one phosphorus to nitrogen signature

00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:00.280
while younger conduits record a distinctly different ratio

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:03.100
after Jupiter's migrations stirred the inventory.

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:06.580
The difference is measurable down to parts per million,

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:09.820
revealing exactly when and where the ingredients

00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:12.100
for oceans and biology were delivered.

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:15.520
Yet the precise timing of Jupiter's first inward

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:18.280
then outward journey remains an open question

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:21.300
that no current sample set can fully pin down.

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:25.040
New chapters in solar system history keep unfolding

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:27.140
from the smallest chemical clues.

